.TH LIBMPQ__STREAM_OPEN_NAME_IDENTITY 3 2026-11-04 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__stream_open_name_identity \- open an exact named member stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>

int32_t libmpq__stream_open_name_identity(
        mpq_archive_s *archive, const char *filename,
        uint16_t locale, uint16_t platform, mpq_stream_s **stream);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open a read-only logical stream for exactly the requested filename identity.
Selection occurs on the owned archive/source clone that backs the stream.
It is never reselected through ordinary name lookup, and no locale-neutral
fallback occurs. The supplied filename is retained for basename-derived
MPQ encryption, including FIX_KEY; no full-path-key fallback is added.
.PP
Compression, single-unit/sector storage, custom read-at sources and MPQE
use the existing stream path. The result survives parent archive closure.
Caller-managed custom callback contexts must outlive dependent streams.
libmpq__stream_close(3) consumes the result. The operation does not close
or modify input archives. Existing ambiguous/reduced identity restrictions
apply. Physical archive checksums and signatures do not become a new trust
claim about logical stream content.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success or a negative libmpq error. A valid output is entirely
cleared on failure. No partial stream is returned.
.SH ERRORS
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates missing required arguments, an absent identity
or the end of enumeration. LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT indicates malformed canonical
mappings, contradictory duplicate identities or unsupported reduced hashes.
Read-only identity queries reject writable archives with
LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED. Stream opening rejects invalid writer handles
with LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. Existing allocation, source I/O and decode errors
are propagated. All source archives remain unchanged.
